land-atlas/oregon/tillamook-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and August to September came in under 90% of normal in 39 of them, more than any other pair. July to August is the driest pair at 2.41 inches normal, and November to December the wettest at 29.23 inches. In 2025 on the middle of the grids, June to July came in at 28% of normal and May to June at 48%. Grid 30027 had its driest year in 2013 at 57% of normal.</p>"}
